WEBVTT

00:00:07.571 --> 00:00:11.024
A job planner can share a name and description while

00:00:11.024 --> 00:00:14.344
each kind of job defines its own time calculation.

00:00:14.344 --> 00:00:17.333
An abstract class holds that shared state and

00:00:17.333 --> 00:00:20.321
behavior, but cannot be constructed directly.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:52.816
ReadingJob extends NamedJob, making it a subclass.

00:00:52.816 --> 00:00:54.683
NamedJob is its superclass.

00:00:54.683 --> 00:00:58.416
The super constructor call initializes the name before

00:00:58.416 --> 00:00:59.315
pages is set.

00:00:59.315 --> 00:01:02.287
The description reuses superclass behavior.

00:01:02.287 --> 00:01:06.020
The heading reads the private name through a protected

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:07.610
getter accessible here.

00:01:07.915 --> 00:01:11.559
The abstract minutes declaration requires ReadingJob

00:01:11.559 --> 00:01:12.751
to supply a body.

00:01:12.751 --> 00:01:15.554
Both variables refer to the same object.

00:01:15.554 --> 00:01:18.638
The NamedJob reference can call its declared

00:01:18.638 --> 00:01:21.861
operations, and the object supplies overridden

00:01:21.861 --> 00:01:22.492
behavior.

00:01:22.492 --> 00:01:25.015
Predict the three lines, then pause.

00:01:29.981 --> 00:01:33.310
The heading uses the stored name, so it prints Job:

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:33.702
Guide.

00:01:33.702 --> 00:01:36.705
The overridden description adds reading to the

00:01:36.705 --> 00:01:38.206
superclass description.

00:01:38.206 --> 00:01:41.600
Three pages at two minutes each produce six minutes.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:44.212
Calls through job still use ReadingJob's

00:01:44.212 --> 00:01:45.256
implementations.

00:01:45.315 --> 00:01:47.421
Change the page count to zero.

00:01:47.421 --> 00:01:49.596
Predict all three output lines.

00:01:49.596 --> 00:01:53.106
Explain which methods depend on the name and which

00:01:53.106 --> 00:01:54.790
method depends on pages.
